================================================================================
ANALYSIS
================================================================================

Key Insight:
  - Morton radius searches along 1D Morton curve (wrong for sparse cells)
  - Grid neighbors searches 3D cube (correct spatial neighbors)

Expected behavior:
  - Random particles in bbox: ~30-50% fall inside mesh (rest in void)
  - For particles INSIDE mesh, grid search should find ~98%
  - Expected overall: ~35% (0.4 × 0.98 ≈ 39%, accounting for void)

Best grid result: Grid neighbors 5×5×5 (radius=2) = 46.2%
Best Morton result: Morton radius=50 = 60.5%

⚠  Grid search not better (needs investigation)

